<article class="env-lemma" id="079S">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/079S">Lemma <span data-tag="079S">20.26.6</span>.</a> Let $(X, \mathcal{O}_ X)$ be a ringed space. Let $(\mathcal{K}_1^\bullet , \mathcal{K}_2^\bullet , \mathcal{K}_3^\bullet )$ be a distinguished triangle in $K(\textit{Mod}(\mathcal{O}_ X))$. If two out of three of $\mathcal{K}_ i^\bullet $ are K-flat, so is the third. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Follows from Lemma <a href="/tag/06Y8" data-tag="06Y8">20.26.1</a> and the fact that in a distinguished triangle in $K(\textit{Mod}(\mathcal{O}_ X))$ if two out of three are acyclic, so is the third. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>